QuestGuidance.Register("en",444,{
[14177]="7000B98B\n1\tBring the shining heartwood to a woodworker in Rivendell\tA woodworker in Rivendell might be able to fashion something of great worth from the shining heartwood you found. You should bring the shining heartwood to a woodworker in Rivendell.\n",
[14178]="7002274D\n1\tSearch for Holfast's Button in the Attic\030Search for Holfast's Pocket-watch in the Main Cellar\030Search for Holfast's Glove in the Cobwebbed Wing\030Search for Holfast's Ring in the Creeping Wing\030Search for Holfast's monocle in the Basement\tHolfast Burrows' missing valuables are probably scattered throughout corners of the Haunted Burrow in places where he hoped to find hidden treasure. You should seek Holfast's missing valuables in the Haunted Burrow.\n2\tReturn the missing valuables to Holfast Burrows\tHolfast Burrows stands outside the Haunted Burrow, near the Party Tree in Hobbiton. You have found all of Holfast's missing valuables, and now you should return them to their master.\n",
[14179]="70036A9D\n1\tDefend the tower from the waves of goblins ([see journal]/8)\tThe Rohirrim need aid in protecting the materials within the siege towers from the vandals ascending the wall. Protect the winch and supply crates from armed powder kegs and prevent allied guards from falling before the blows of the enemy. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[14180]="700381C3\n1\tDefend the towers from waves of goblins ([see journal]/24)\tThe Rohirrim need aid in protecting the materials within the siege towers from the vandals ascending the wall. Protect the winch and supply crates from armed powder kegs and prevent allied guards from falling before the blows of the enemy. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[14181]="7006C12B\n1\tInvestigate the marsh of Zahûmakh for signs of the travellers\tInvestigate Zahûmakh for signs of the travellers.\n2\tAid wounded travellers (total: 4)\030Recover traveller's packs (total: 4)\030Defeat marsh-striders (total: 7)\tAid the travellers, grab their packs, and fight off any marsh-striders who get in your way.\n3\tMake your way out of Zahûmakh\tMake your way out of Zahûmakh.\n4\tDefeat Luhum-gêna\tDefeat Luhum-gêna, queen of the marsh.\n",
[14182]="700700C4\n1\tFind Ponto Underhill's shovel\030Find Sarabeth Lowbanks's book\030Find Ferdibrand Took's pipe\030Find Ethelinda Burr's teapot\030Find Ferumbras Attereeve's lucky tankard\030Find Pell Stoneleaf's whittling knife\tFredegunda believes cave-claw burglars have stolen each of the missing items and maintains that the items could all be found inside the tunnel to the south-east of the village centre.\n2\tReturn Ponto Underhill's shovel\030Return Sarabeth Lowbanks's book\030Return Ferdibrand Took's pipe\030Return Ethelinda Burr's teapot\030Return Ferumbras Attereeve's lucky tankard\030Return Pell Stoneleaf's whittling knife\tInside the tunnel, you have found each of the items Fredegunda Cutt believed you would. You should return each of the items to their owners in the village of Staddle.\n3\tTalk to Fredegunda Cutt\tYou have returned the stolen items to their respective owners. You should return to Fredegunda Cutt in Staddle and tell her what happened.\n",
[14183]="70016BA4\n1\tBogrian's mirror is at Dâr-rukh, atop a tall Moria-mirror tower which overlooks the morroval-caverns to the east. Folkath believes the time has come to strike against the morroval-queen. He knows she has an ancient mirror she values highly, and Folkath believes if you were to tamper with it, Bogrian will appear and attack.\t\n2\tTalk to Folkath at the Fanged Pit camp\tFolkath as at the camp on the western edge of the morroval-caverns. Folkath will be pleased to hear that you wounded Bogrian and forced her to retreat from the battle.\n",
[14184]="700456A5\n1\tDefeat Variags in Bâr Nadhron (total: 12)\tYou should defeat Variags in Bâr Nadhron in the Beacon Hills of Far Anórien.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have defeated many Variags in Bâr Nadhron.\n",
[14185]="700006BE\n1\tDefeat Rhudauran Hillmen loyal to the Red-maid (total: 8)\tThe Hillmen of Rhudaur can be found within Agamaur, the Red Swamp. Dannasen, sent you to bring vengeance upon the Hillmen of Rhudaur, who serve the Red-maid. He asked you to deliver vengeance upon them for the pain and suffering that their ancestors caused upon the land and the same which they do even now.\n2\tTalk to Dannasen\tDannasen is at the Eglan-camp in Agamaur. Unwilling to yield, the Rhudauran Hillmen fought you on sight. Dannasen's request completed, the time has come to return to him.\n",
[14186]="7002F640\n1\tDefeat mounted Orcs around Elthengels (total: 6)\tOrc-riders can be found in the fields north and west of Elthengels in the Norcrofts. The mounted Orcs around Elthengels have been responsible for many casualties and much suffering.\n2\tCompleted\tThe people of Elthengels will greatly benefit from having fewer Orc-riders to harass them.\n",
[14187]="700455E0\n1\tMeet the Riders Three at Erelas\tErelas can be found north-east of Ost Rimmon. The Riders Three have asked you to meet them at the beacon-hill Erelas.\n2\tTalk to Burnoth at Erelas\030Talk to Hutha at Erelas\030Talk to Ulf at Erelas\tBurnoth, Hutha, and Ulf are at the beacon-hill Erelas. You have arrived at Erelas and should now speak to the Riders Three about the truth of Léofdag's demise.\n3\tMeet the Riders Three at their camp in Taur Drúadan\tThe Riders Three can be found somewhere among the War-stead of the King's Men in Taur Drúadan. The Riders Three have asked you to join them in their quest and their journey to the Pelennor Fields.\n4\tTalk to Burnoth in Taur Drúadan\tBurnoth is at his camp within the War-stead of the King's Men. You have arrived in Taur Drúadan and should now speak to Burnoth.\n",
[14188]="70000044\n1\tDefeat White Hand Guards (total: 8)\030Defeat White Hand Spear-throwers (total: 8)\030Defeat White Hand Thrasher\tGoblins can be found in the ruins of Minas Eriol, south-east of The Forsaken Inn. Goblins slaughtered many of the Eglain, and Gadaric Munce wants to revisit these losses upon the evil creatures. He bade you go to the ruins where the attack took place and defeat any goblins you find there.\n2\tTalk to Gadaric Munce\tGadaric Munce is at The Forsaken Inn. You found your prey within the ruins and dispatched them, avenging those of the Eglain slain at the hands of the goblins. Gadaric Munce will wish to hear of your victory.\n",
[14189]="70058B8A\n1\tCollect 'medallions' of Gorgar at Azgh-buzru (total: 15)\030Collect dwarf-beard trophies at Azgh-buzru (total: 8)\tDwarf-beards are kept as trophies by Orcs at Azgh-buzru. Medallions are carried by Orcs, trolls, and goblins loyal to Gorgar the Ruthless at Azgh-buzru. Mézto has asked you to reclaim dwarf-beards taken as trophies by the forces of Gundabad. In addition, Mézto has asked to you collect the crude medallions carried by those loyal to Gorgar the Ruthless.\n2\tDeliver the 'medallions' and dwarf-beards to Mézto at Drenghól\tMézto can be found at Drenghól in the War of Three Peaks. You have collected many trophies from the forces of Gundabad. You should deliver them to Mézto at Drenghól.\n",
[14190]="700096FD\n1\tConfront Brychan the Bold\tBrychan the Bold is at his home in Ost Forod, north-east of Tinnudir. Helechír told you to return to the mainland and follow the road north of the cross-roads of Canadiach until you reach Ost Forod. Helechír has asked you to confront Brychan the Bold about the many crimes his gang of tomb-robbers have committed.\n2\tTalk to Helechír\tHelechír is on a little island off of Men Erain. You taught Brychan the Bold a hard lesson, and he fled into his home. Helechír is waiting to hear the tale of your confrontation with the leader of the robber-gang.\n",
[14191]="70065F7A\n1\tTalk to Londring\tThe wharf master has asked you to speak with Londring to see if anyone has come by to borrow tools or use the workbench. Londring is in the Artisans' Quarter, in Dol Amroth.\n2\tTalk to someone at the stables\tLondring had a rude encounter with Yârlag, who seems to have gone in search of a horse. You should check the stables near Harper's Court to see if anyone there met with the brute. Harper's Court is in Dol Amroth.\n3\tSearch for Yârlag\tMellien also had a rude encounter with Yârlag, who ran off towards Harper's Court. You should look for Yârlag in Dol Amroth's Harper's Court.\n4\tExamine the spilled ale\tWhile searching for Yârlag, you discovered a spilled mug of ale. You should investigate the mug. The mug is in Harper's Court, in Dol Amroth.\n5\tReturn to Annúngil\tWhile searching Harper's Court, you found and defeated Yârlag. You should let the wharf master know that he will no longer be sabotaging the Rosigil or any other ships. The wharf master is on the docks in Dol Amroth's bay.\n",
[14192]="70047BED\n1\tTalk to Faramir at Dol Acharn\tFaramir can be found at the foot of Dol Acharn in north-eastern Dagorlad. Faramir has asked you to confront Burudagath the Bloodletter at Ondoher's Folly. You should speak to him when you are ready to depart.\n2\tTalk to Anborn at Haerondir\tAnborn can be found at Haerondir in the Wastes. You have defeated Burudagath the Bloodletter and should now bring tidings of victory to Anborn.\n3\tTalk to Faramir at Haerondir\tFaramir can be found near Anborn at Haerondir in the Wastes. Faramir has suddenly appeared at your side at Haerondir. You should speak to him and learn why he has come.\n4\tTalk to Anborn at Haerondir\tAnborn can be found at Haerondir. Faramir, son of Ondoher has come to the old ruins of Haerondir and intends to aid the Rangers in maintaining the illusion that the ruins are haunted. You should now speak to Anborn again.\n",
[14193]="70066007\n1\tSearch for Dúnach\tLothon has asked you to look for his companion, Dúnach. You should search Calembel for signs of the missing prison guard.\n2\tInvestigate the area around the guard's body\tWhile searching for Dúnach, you found their body. You should examine the area around the body for any signs of a clue. You found the body in Calembel.\n3\tFollow the trail of blood\tSadly, while searching for Dúnach, you found their body. After examining the area, a trail of blood was discovered! It looks like Dúnach went down fighting. You should follow the trail of blood. The trail of blood is in Calembel.\n4\tTalk to the injured woman\tFollowing the trail of blood led you to an angry, injured woman. She glares up at you, waiting for you to approach. You should question the injured woman. The injured woman is in a small hamlet outside of Calembel.\n5\tTalk to Lord Angbor\tGorneth has confessed to the murder of Dúnach, and given you an accounts book detailing the prison guard's many crimes. She has asked that you pass the book along to Lord Angbor. Lord Angbor is in Calembel.\n",
[14194]="70027F15\n1\tCollect Orc-weapons (total: 12)\tOrc-weapons can be found on the Orcs throughout the mines. Edhere asked you to collect weapons for the slaves held in the Orc-mines to use during their escape.\n2\tBring the collected weapons to Edhere\tEdhere is in the Orc-mines. You should bring the weapons you collected to Edhere.\n",
[14195]="70007B46\n1\tDeliver the poison-sacs to Stanric at Ost Guruth\030Collect poison sacs (total: 8)\tRuin-web hunters and ambushers dwell within the ruins of Amon Ros, west of Ost Guruth. Stanric explained that spider-venom could be used to create a medicine against poisons and possibly save lives. He sent you to Amon Ros to collect poison from the spiders there.\n",
[14196]="7002EA85\n1\tDefeat Venomtongue, eldest of the great salamanders\tA cruel old salamander by the name of Venomtongue has roamed these ruins for far too long. You should defeat Venomtongue, for he has been allowed to endure for too many long years.\n2\tDefeat Venomtongue, eldest of the great salamanders\tA cruel old salamander by the name of Venomtongue has roamed these ruins for far too long. You should defeat Venomtongue, for he has been allowed to endure for too many long years.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have defeated one of the most vicious salamanders in the Wold, old Venomtongue of the Seething Mire.\n",
[14197]="7000E3FC\n1\tTalk to Ora\tPynti-peldot lies far to the north of Kauppa-kohta, past a great ice chasm. You were told to speak with the chieftain at Pynti-peldot.\n",
[14198]="7001161F\n1\tTalk to Ora\tPynti-peldot lies far to the north of Kauppa-kohta, past a great ice chasm. You were told to speak with the chieftain at Pynti-peldot.\n",
[14199]="70071B34\n1\tDefeat gredbyg at the Slopes of Shâlahin (total: 8)\tYou should defeat gredbyg on the Slopes of Shâlahin in An Shêru, south-west of Jiret-menêsh.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have defeated many gredbyg on the Slopes of Shâlahin in An Shêru, south-west of Jiret-menêsh.\n",
[14200]="7003EB08\n1\tDefeat cave-claws in the South Trollshaws (total: 8)\tThere are cave-claws infesting the South Trollshaws. While you are in the South Trollshaws, you should cull the number of cave-claws infesting the ruins and low-lands.\n",
[14201]="70063D96\n1\tSpeak with Tordúr to travel to the Heart of Baranzibar\tIf you are willing, speak with Tordúr and make your way to the Heart if Baranzibar. Fight the forces of Angmar there.\n2\tComplete a battle within the Heart of Baranzibar\tFight against the encroaching forces of Angmar in the depths of Moria.\n3\tTalk to Captain-General Tordúr\tWith the battle complete, you should return to Tordúr and tell them of your effort.\n",
[14202]="70063D99\n1\tSpeak with Uglash to travel to the Heart of Baranzibar\tA simple task. Speak with Uglash to travel to the Heart of Baranzibar in Moria. There, fight off the Free People who would take this treasured hall away from your allies.\n2\tComplete a Battle in the Heart of Baranzibar\tFight against the encroaching Free People in the depths of Moria. Speak with again to make the journey swiftly.\n3\tTalk to Uglash\tAfter fighting in the depths of Moria, there is only one thing left to do. Speak with Uglash and tell them how the battle went.\n",
[14203]="7003FFF5\n1\tDefeat rats (total: 6)\tThe rats must be dealt with to save the food supplies in the warehouse.\n",
[14204]="70002E1E\n1\tDefeat Stone-trolls in the South Trollshaws\tStone-trolls can be found north of the road, eastward from the Last Bridge and Barachen's camp. You should dispatch the Stone-trolls which have come down from the mountains, for their migration into the Trollshaws poses a danger to all who pass that way.\n2\tDefeat Stone-trolls in the South Trollshaws (total: 6)\tStone-trolls can be found north of the road, eastward from the Last Bridge and Barachen's camp. You should dispatch the Stone-trolls which have come down from the mountains, for their migration into the Trollshaws poses a danger to all who pass that way.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have defeated many Stone-trolls in the South Trollshaws.\n",
[14205]="70028264\n1\tTalk to Mair among the cairns\tMair is posted among the cairns in the Bonevales. You should bring the remnants of the vessel to Mair.\n",
[14206]="70000628\n1\tCollect the Urn of Agamaur\tThe urn is in the south-western part of Agamaur. The shade Dannasen has asked you to recover the Red-maid's urn, fill it with water from an ancient, natural altar, and bring it back to him.\n2\tFill the Urn of Agamaur\030Find the Red-maid's altar\tThe altar is in the south-eastern part of Agamaur. Fill the urn you collected with water from the area surrounding a natural altar guarded by darkwater.\n3\tSpeak with Dannasen\030Collect The Filled Urn of Agamaur\tDannasen is at the Eglain camp, north-west of the Red-maid's altar. Now that you have filled the urn with water from the area surrounding the altar, you should return to Dannasen.\n",
[14207]="70025B36\n1\tCollect vases at Tham Varan (total: 4)\tTham Varan is east of Tinnudir and Tham Nambarth. You should go to Tham Varan and collect several vases for the Rangers of Tinnudir.\n2\tBring the vases to Nadfaron\tThe Rangers are at Tinnudir, west of Tham Varan and Tham Nambarth. One of the Rangers will be excited to begin examining the contents of the vases you found at Tham Varan.\n",
[14208]="7002F6C4\n1\tRetrieve Pendrad's shield\030Retrieve Pendrad's sword\tThe missing items from Thane Pendrad can likely be found among the fields of Orcs to the north and west of Elthengels. You have found the late Thane Pendrad's helmet and are now looking for other lost weapons or armour that may have belonged to him.\n2\tReturn Pendrad's belongings to Thane Mildrith\tThane Mildrith awaits you at the Elthengels Mead Hall, on the eastern edge of the Norcrofts. You have recovered the lost items of the late Thane Pendrad and should return them to his widow, Thane Mildrith.\n",
})
